    story: Duarte Cryptthorn entered the world in a forge quarter blackened by smoke
      and debt, surrounded by people who measured children through quiet restraint.
      Years in dusty library rooms watched by tired scholars gave Duarte Cryptthorn
      habits that looked strange to outsiders and useful to anyone who understood
      restlessness that kept looking for a door. In a bandit season where trust was
      expensive, Duarte Cryptthorn learned that a future could be bought with bruises,
      discipline, and cruelty learned as protection.
